    "title": "5 Big Ideas for Sioux Falls' Empty Royal Fork Building - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ben Kuhns ,\n22 minutes ago\nAugust of this year marked five years since the beloved local buffet restaurant at the Empire Mall Sioux Falls, The Royal Fork, closed. The building where it made its home since 1993 still sits empty, as of September 2025.\nThe former Royal Fork building is located at 4610 W Empire Place in Sioux Falls, on the campus of The Empire Mall. It could be a great spot for a new business. It’s right in the middle of probably the busiest part of Sioux Falls.\nSo, what should go into this building? Or how about the space itself? We asked around and here are some of the best ideas.\nRead More: Remember The Iconic Sioux Falls Tomato Soup from Royal Fork?\nDownload the KKLS Mobile App Now Royal Fork building in 2019, located at 4610 W Empire Place in Sioux Falls (Google Maps Streetview) Click here to view photo gallery Click here to view photo gallery",
